AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::setCreditLimit()
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
├── when new credit limit is zero and no debt exists
│   └── it should accrue interest and set the credit limit to zero
├── when new credit limit exceeds uint128 max
│   └── it should accrue and then revert with MathUtilsMaxUint128Overflow during checked conversion
├── given market is not paused
│   ├── it should accrue interest before comparing the new limit with debt
│   ├── when IRM accrual fails
│   │   └── it should revert without changing the credit limit
│   └── when accrued debt exceeds the proposed limit
│       └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInsufficientMarketLiquidity and roll back accrual
├── given market is paused
│   ├── it should skip interest accrual regardless of elapsed time
│   └── it should compare the proposed limit with currently recorded active debt plus badDebtAssets
├── when new credit limit is less than active debt plus badDebtAssets
│   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInsufficientMarketLiquidity
├── when new credit limit equals active debt plus badDebtAssets
│   └── it should succeed
└── when new credit limit is valid
    ├── it should permit increases and decreases at or above active debt plus badDebtAssets
    ├── it should restore only the capacity above badDebtAssets when increased after foreclosure
    ├── it should accept exactly uint128 max
    ├── when new value equals current credit limit
    │   └── it should still emit and leave the same value
    ├── it should update totalSupply assets
    ├── it should leave totalSupply shares at zero
    ├── it should not change totalBorrowed shares positions claimableFeesAssets or badDebtAssets except through accrual
    └── it should emit SetCreditLimit with old and new values after any AccrueInterest event
